    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>The insurance adjuster, staff or independent, works for and is paid by the insurance company. A public adjuster is hired by and works for the policyholder.</li>
<li>You pay nothing to the insurer’s adjuster. A public adjuster’s fee is set in a written contract, and Texas caps it at 10% of the insurance settlement.</li>
<li>On a storm claim, both adjusters may inspect the same roof. The public adjuster documents and presents the claim; the insurer’s adjuster evaluates it and recommends payment.</li>
<li>Texas Insurance Code Chapter 4102 sets the rules for public adjusters, including a 72-hour right to rescind and a ban on doing the repairs.</li>
